# Frontend Formatting

The frontend uses Prettier for formatting. The pre-commit hooks run `prettier --check`, which will fail if code is not formatted exactly as Prettier expects.

## Enforcement

After editing any frontend file, you MUST run the following command from the `frontend/` directory before ending your turn:

```bash
npm run format
```

This ensures that your changes match the project's formatting standards and will pass CI/pre-commit checks.

## Address Failures

If `npm run format` reports changes, it has auto-fixed the files. If it fails for other reasons (e.g., syntax errors), you must fix them before proceeding.
